WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.175
DAO members cannot review every proposal.

2
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.912
Delegating to one person gives them all the discretion.

3
00:00:07.937 --> 00:00:13.250
VoteMirror offers a clear policy: mirror a vote only when a chosen group
agrees.

4
00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:20.825
This workspace follows Alice, Bob, and Carol, with a two-of-three threshold.

5
00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:25.312
The holder keeps their tokens and delegates voting power to VoteMirror.

6
00:00:25.337 --> 00:00:29.875
The owner can pause mirroring, skip a proposal, or vote directly.

7
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:37.450
Now we are following a fresh proposal on Base Sepolia.

8
00:00:37.475 --> 00:00:42.025
Test ballots are submitted using the project's encrypted demo wallets.

9
00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:44.100
Alice votes For.

10
00:00:44.125 --> 00:00:48.025
One ballot is below the threshold, so VoteMirror waits.

11
00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:50.375
Bob also votes For.

12
00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:55.162
Reactive observes the Governor's events on Lasna and requests a callback.

13
00:00:55.187 --> 00:01:01.400
Back on Base, VoteMirror checks the ordered ballot receipts and current
policy before casting its vote.

14
00:01:01.425 --> 00:01:04.950
The Governor now records the mirrored voting power.

15
00:01:04.975 --> 00:01:08.375
Only trusted addresses count toward the threshold.

16
00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:13.512
The holder's voting power is used once, while the tokens remain in their own
wallet.

17
00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:26.637
These explorer pages show the proof.

18
00:01:26.662 --> 00:01:29.550
The source ballot is on Base Sepolia.

19
00:01:29.575 --> 00:01:35.112
Its matching Lasna notification carries the same origin transaction hash and
log data.

20
00:01:35.137 --> 00:01:41.900
The destination transaction goes through the callback proxy and records
VoteMirror's result and the Governor's vote event.

21
00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:59.412
Recorded tests cover disagreement, owner skips, paused delivery, retries,
and an owner voting first.

22
00:01:59.437 --> 00:02:02.837
Split choices do not combine into agreement.

23
00:02:02.862 --> 00:02:05.775
A skip prevents an automated vote.

24
00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:09.362
An extra ballot does not create a duplicate vote.

25
00:02:09.387 --> 00:02:13.900
The evidence index links every tested path to its transactions.

26
00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:28.387
A separate recovery sender can restore eligible votes when event delivery is
unavailable.

27
00:02:28.412 --> 00:02:32.225
That path is labeled separately from Reactive callbacks.

28
00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:38.775
This is a testnet demonstration; delivery depends on network access, fee
funding, and the voting deadline.

29
00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:43.512
VoteMirror: your trusted circle, your voting power, your final say.
